In today’s hyper connected world, the NGN framework serves as the foundation for integrating voice, video, data, and emerging services such as cloud native applications, IoT connectivity, and immersive media. By consolidating diverse communication signals onto a unified IP based platform, operators can achieve greater network agility, reduced operational expenditures, and the ability to deliver differentiated services at scale.
What is Next Generation Network (NGN) ?
NGN refers to an IP based communication architecture that supersedes traditional circuit centric and legacy *MPLS and PSTN infrastructures. It encompasses a fully virtualized core, programmable transport, and a service oriented edge, enabling operators to dynamically provision resources, enforce quality of service guarantees, and accelerate the rollout of new applications. Fundamentally, NGN combines high‐capacity fiber backbones, 5G core technologies, and software defined networking to create an end to end architecture that supports distributed, latency sensitive workloads.
